| # | File | What was wrong | What is fixed |
|---|------|----------------|---------------|
| 1 | `CaseSurveyJob.cls` | `implements System.Queueable` with `execute(System.Queueable context)` — `System.Queueable` (capital Q, no `Context` suffix) is the *interface*, not the *parameter type*. | Changed parameter type to `System.QueueableContext context`, matching the compiler-reported method signature `System.Queueable.execute(System.QueueableContext)`. |
| 2 | `CaseTrigger.trigger` | Had a `break` at 50 enqueues, silently discarding surveys for cases beyond the 50th in a single transaction — violating the spec that **every** qualifying case must get its own job. | Removed the `break` / silent skip. Every qualifying case gets `System.enqueueJob(...)`. The 50-per-transaction governor limit is documented as a caller / integration concern in the trigger header comment with two concrete mitigations (chunk API batches to ≤ 50, or add a `BatchApex` fan-out wrapper). |

